SUMMARY:Cove Creek/Caney Bottom Loop\; the hike
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the ***HFF Trail Trekkers***: We a
 ’gonna get our step-counters a’workin’ !!\nHugh will lead on the Cov
 e Crk Falls and Caney Bottoms Falls\, Up to 10 of you are welcome to join 
 him.\n\\*\\*PARTICIPANTS REQUIRE THE APPROVAL OF THE HIKE ORGANIZER.\\*\\*
 \nLength: 6.5 mi Total\; Accum ascent: 700ft\nPace: 2.5mph\nDifficulty: we
 ll established trail\; challenging short steep slopes to bases of falls.\n
 **WET STREAM XINGS\; BE PREPARED !!!**\n**Optional: swimming at the Campgr
 ound Sliding Rock Pool.**\n**Masticating will be ‘in motion’.**\nDrive
  time: 15 min (1-way).\nApprx return time: 2\;30 pm\nCarpool contributions
  appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Brevard\, NC\nWAITLISTED PEO
 PLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 3 drivers. (=12ppl
 )\n**Please bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy shoe
 s into the driver's car at the end of the hike.**\n**We suggest open windo
 ws while carpooling.**\nDESCRIPTION\;\nThis hike takes you on a loop past 
 several nice waterfalls. Climbs moderately overall\; some of the first cli
 mbs are very steep but short. Mostly easy trails with one rough section up
  from Cove Creek Falls to the trail. Beautiful Pisgah scenery and lush woo
 ds abound\, and travels through some nice flats above the Davidson River v
 alley at the base of the Pisgah Ridge. Passes seepage bogs and fern-filled
  open woods.\nAll hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your
  OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: The organizer of this event i
 s a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer 
 is only to organize this event. There are certain risks inherent in any ou
 tdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, ag
 rees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Par
 tners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or 
 personal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or wh
 ile traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further 
 agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow
  instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated
  from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images coll
 ected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\nHugh's con
 tact: (**before** day of hike): (662) 324-2425 (text only)\n**Pics: https:
 //www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
